WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.570
What does the fictional drug Drops do, exactly?

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.990
Is it new to the Batman mythos?

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:08.309
And how will it play into The Penguin's criminal
ambitions?

00:00:08.309 --> 00:00:11.410
Keep watching for what we know and where we
think things might go.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.179
Warning: Spoilers for "The Batman" ahead.

00:00:14.179 --> 00:00:17.760
The Gotham City that director Matt Reeves
brings to life in "The Batman" is a place

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.180
where corrupt politicians and law enforcement
work hand-in-dirty-hand with the real rulers

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:25.500
of the town, who live outside the law and
pay enough to keep it that way.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.710
From gang wars to money laundering, it's a
challenging place to keep in check.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:33.309
Things only get stranger when the mayor gets
killed by a creepy criminal mastermind who

00:00:33.309 --> 00:00:37.329
loves riddles and the only reliable figure
in town is struggling to be taken seriously

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:39.539
because he dresses like a bat.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.539
"I'm vengeance."

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:43.320
The Gotham of "The Batman" also has a serious
drug problem.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.460
This new drug on the streets, referred to
as "Drops," is impacting every rung of the

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.670
social ladder.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.719
But just what are these so-called Drops?

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:54.860
Though there are some fictional drugs that
pop up in comics and other media, Drops don't

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.910
appear in the more than eight decades of Batman's
history.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:02.139
This is a new fictional drug devised by Reeves
and co-writer Peter Craig, presented within

00:01:02.139 --> 00:01:04.199
the first few minutes of the new film.

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:08.290
Applied by the user like a simple eye drop,
the drug causes hyperactivity and paranoia,

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:13.020
as shown by District Attorney Gil Colson when
he's speaking to Selina at 44 Below.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:16.460
The substance's impact on the city continues
throughout the film.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:20.409
It's a festering issue bubbling underneath
Batman's greater challenge of battling the

00:01:20.409 --> 00:01:23.389
Riddler and uncovering the corruption that
permeates the city.

00:01:23.389 --> 00:01:27.340
From Penguin's thwarted distribution scheme,
to Batman and Gordon encountering so-called

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:31.840
"Drop heads" holing up in the abandoned orphanage,
Batman's war on Drops in Gotham continues

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.380
to rage on, even after he's called a hero.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.119
For now, there aren't any answers about this
drug's future.

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:42.469
However, a future spin-off series on HBO Max
about The Penguin may just provide new answers.

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:46.970
When last we see him, Colin Farrell's Oswald
Cobblepot, aka The Penguin, is looking at

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:51.631
a flooded Gotham City, and seeing a new dawn,
with a wide-open space for a new crime boss

00:01:51.631 --> 00:01:54.659
to take over Carmine Falcone's former empire.

00:01:54.659 --> 00:01:58.600
It stands to reason, then, that the Penguin
spin-off will focus on precisely that, as

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:02.880
Cobblepot fights his way to the top of the
criminal empire, eventually reaching his inevitable

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:03.960
archvillain status.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.450
A crime boss has got to make money somehow,
and chances are that Drops will continue to

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:10.420
be a crucial part of his operation.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:14.360
Still, a business like this is tough, with
the competition even more so.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:18.780
It's a safe bet that Mr. Cobblepot could have
a gang war on the horizon.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.370
Speaking to Hero Nation, Reeves revealed that
the upcoming show would take inspiration from

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:26.540
the likes of machine-gun-toting gangster gem
"Scarface" and British crime classic "The

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.659
Long Good Friday."

00:02:27.659 --> 00:02:31.720
Both films saw their lead character at the
top of their organizations, forced to go head-on

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.379
with competition, with unpleasant results
for both.

00:02:34.379 --> 00:02:36.640
"Say hello to my little friend!"

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.670
The series is likely to see the Penguin make
new enemies — the kind that don't have pointy

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:41.670
bat ears.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:45.220
Perhaps, a form of competition could arise
in the form of another drug.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:49.400
Namely, could the drug Venom be making its
way to the world of "The Batman," and with

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.980
it, it's most famous user, Bane?

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.769
Many fans theorized that the green liquid
Batman pumped himself with to save Selina

00:02:55.769 --> 00:03:00.230
was Venom, the go-to drug used by Bane in
the comics to increase his strength.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:04.110
While it hasn't been confirmed whether this
was the mysterious green goo or it was simply

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:08.170
a shot of adrenaline, seeing Venom enter the
world of "The Batman" could lead to some exciting

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.170
conflict.

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:13.260
Perhaps this version of Bane would be a little
closer to the comics than the Tom Hardy incarnation

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.920
in "The Dark Knight Rises."

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:19.980
Could the Penguin's HBO Max spin-off see Cobblepot's
operation get muscled over by Bane?

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:23.450
In the process, could we find out the origins
of Drops and their manufacturer?

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:27.350
After all, we never did find out what the
character who is now confirmed to be The Joker

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:28.920
was in Arkham for.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.950
The arrival of Venom, some other new drug,
or competing crime bosses could definitely

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:36.319
spell trouble for Cobblepot's now-flooded
empire.

